SUMMARY:LBC Bike to 30K Program: How to Shift Your Bike with Trek Bikes 
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nThe Bike to 30K is hostin
 g a class with Trek Bikes on How To Shift. Join us for this informational 
 program.\n\n**Grab your helmets\, bikes\, and sneakers — Lancaster Bicyc
 le Club is gearing up for beginner and transitional rides!** Local members
  of the LBC are thrilled to host this year’s **Bike to 30K Program**\, d
 esigned especially for new\, returning\, and curious cyclists.\n\n## **Abo
 ut the Program**\n\nBike to 30K is a seven‑week series that gently build
 s your confidence\, fitness\, and mileage. We begin with a five‑mile rid
 e and gradually work up to eighteen miles by the end of the program. Our g
 oal is simple: to introduce riders of all experience levels to the joy of 
 cycling in a supportive\, community‑focused environment.\nThis program i
 s **FREE** with an LBC membership — and membership is also free. The Bik
 e to 30K program is open to everyone in our community who wants to ride.\n
 \n## **Why We Ride**\n\nEver wonder why cyclists keep coming back? Because
  it’s fun. There’s nothing like coasting downhill and letting out a bi
 g “weeeeeee” all the way to the bottom. But we also know that if you
 ’re new to cycling\, jumping straight into an 18‑mile ride can feel in
 timidating. That’s exactly why Bike to 30K exists.\nEach week\, you’ll
  increase your mileage at a comfortable pace. You’ll get to know the clu
 b\, meet fellow riders\, and gradually grow into a confident **Fun Rider**
  — the group known for enjoying scenic\, social rides together.\n\n## **
 Our Commitment to You**\n\nLancaster Bicycle Club is dedicated to supporti
 ng new riders and helping our community reach their cycling goals. Bike to
  30K is part of our initiative to encourage more people to get outside\, g
 et active\, and discover how enjoyable cycling can be.\nSpend seven weeks 
 with us and watch yourself transform into a Fun Rider — one mile at a ti
 me.\nThe Bike to 30K program is voluntary\, welcoming\, and designed with 
 beginners in mind. We can’t wait to ride with you.\n\n## **Membership\, 
 Waiver & RSVP Requirements**\n\nTo eliminate passing around a pen‑and‑
 paper waiver\, we require both:\n\n* **LBC Club Membership**\, and\n* **Me
 etup RSVP**\n\nYour RSVP allows us to contact you after the ride if needed
 . Please note: **ONLY club members who RSVP are covered by the club’s ex
 cess accident insurance policy.** Being on Meetup does *not* mean you are 
 a club member. To join our wonderful club\, please sign up through our mem
 bership link.\n\n##
