SUMMARY:Annapolis Trail Ride 34 Flat RSVP Required
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nthere's still time for yo
 u to sign up for this bicycle ride. as of now both groups we have six ride
 rs. come join us Saturday. Time for one of our favorite rides….Join your
  friends from the Lancaster Club and the Wilmington Club ….Annapolis Fri
 end Trail Ride will be held on Saturday\, April 18…. the Annapolis Trail
  34F at 11mph pace.\nLancaster Club at 8:30am we will leave the parking lo
 t of Rutter’s Gas off of the Mt Zion exit of route 30 south\, heading in
 to York. From Rutter’s we will car pool to the entrance of the Annapolis
  Trail in Glen Bernie\, Maryland. From the parking lot we will ride the14 
 mile trail\, from the trail on the highway\, picture taking at the monumen
 t\, and then across the bridge in Annapolis.\nFor those coming from the 
 “Rails and Trails Club\,” you may wish to go directly to the Pascal Se
 nior Center parking lot\, 125 Dorsey Rd\; Glen Bernie between 9:45-10am. 
 …the first parking lot. (not in the back.) We will ride as a group with 
 stops along the way\, no one left behind. In Annapolis we will shop/eat/wa
 tch the boats along the water front\, and afterwards return to the trail t
 o ride back to the parking lot and then home. We should arrive back at the
  senior center by 5:00pm. Like all rides you need to wear a helmet and hav
 e a tube so someone can change your flat tire. The trail is paved. Any kin
 d of bicycle will do.\nHelmets are required. Please do not put the leader 
 in an embarrassing position of begging someone to wear a helmet.\nDo not s
 ign up for this ride unless you promise to ride with the group. No one lef
 t behind.\nRSVP required for riders and guests. For more information call 
 Richard Conner\, 717-572-8480
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3142291
 47/
